6. Conclusion

The analysis identified patterns in transaction amounts, categories, timing, geography, and customer demographics that were associated with fraud-labelled transactions.

High-value transactions and late-night transactions showed notably higher fraud rates in this dataset. Transaction distance showed very similar averages between legitimate and fraud-labelled transactions.

These findings are descriptive, not proof of causation or a predictive fraud-detection model.

7. Dataset Limitation

The dataset is simulated and does not represent actual bank or credit card customer transactions. The fraud labels are supplied by the dataset and were used for descriptive analysis only.

June 2020 contains partial-month data and should be interpreted carefully when comparing monthly transaction volumes.
